# What the loaded EPDDL domain declares.
#
# The problem expert answers what is true; the epistemic state answers what is
# known. Neither answers what the domain says can be done, and for an epistemic
# domain that is a different question from the PDDL one: an action is an event
# model with per-agent observability, and none of that has a PDDL surface to be
# read off. `get domain actions` on the classical terminal is blind to all of
# it.
#
# This is the domain-side counterpart, and it answers about EPDDL because EPDDL
# is what the system plans over.
---
bool success
string error

# The problem and domain names the task was ground from, empty when the
# grounding recorded none.
string domain_name
string problem_name

# The agents the domain declares. These are the ones a knowledge formula may
# name, and asking about any other is an error and not a fresh symbol.
string[] agents

# The atoms, which are the propositional vocabulary every formula is written
# in.
string[] atoms

# The grounded actions, by the name the planner searches over. This is the
# vocabulary an action mapping is keyed by.
string[] actions

# Which of those are sensing actions, in the same order as `actions`. A sensing
# action has more than one designated event, so which one occurred has to be
# observed before a policy can continue.
bool[] sensing

# The frame the model is interpreted in: true for KD45 (belief), false for S5
# (knowledge). It decides whether an agent's accessibility must be serial, and
# so whether believing something falsely is expressible at all.
bool kd45

# True when some action gives different agents different observability, which
# is what makes a domain partially observable in the epistemic sense.
bool partial_obs
